<GuideLayout 
  title="Seamless vs Cut-and-Sew: Choosing the Right Construction"
  type="CONSTRUCTION"
  description="Deep dive into manufacturing techniques. Understand which construction method suits your design, budget, and target market."
>
  <p>The construction method defines the look, feel, and cost of your activewear.</p>
  <h3>Cut-and-Sew Manufacturing</h3>
  <p>The traditional method where fabric panels are cut and sewn together. Ideal for complex designs, multiple colors, and specific silhouettes.</p>
  <h3>Seamless Manufacturing</h3>
  <p>Knitted as a tube on specialized machines. Offers superior comfort, maximum stretch, and a "second skin" feel. Best for yoga and high-intensity training.</p>
  <h3>Which to Choose?</h3>
  <p>If you prioritize design versatility, go with cut-and-sew. If you prioritize comfort and high-tech appeal, seamless is the winner.</p>
</GuideLayout>
